+ * `token` is 32 cryptographic random bytes as exactly 43 canonical unpadded base64url characters, minted
+ * per attempt by the host. `frameId` is the renderer's own 36-character UUID from the frame receipt. Every
+ * marker is at most {@link NATIVE_PRESENT_MARKER_MAX_BYTES} bytes.
+ *
+ * The token is not a security boundary against a same-process or same-UID actor: it distinguishes *this*
+ * armed attempt's markers from marker-like bytes that arrive from anywhere else, which is what a host needs
+ * to avoid acting on terminal text it does not own.
+ *
+ * {@link NativePresentMarkerDecoder} is a framing decoder and deliberately not a VT, key or screen parser.
+ * It recognizes exactly the markers of the token it is armed with, reproduces every other byte verbatim,
+ * and retains at most {@link NATIVE_PRESENT_MARKER_MAX_BYTES} bytes between calls. One implementation is
+ * exported so a host and its tests never drift into two subtly different parsers.
+ */
